  "confirmed_defect": "amplify() and polynomial() constructed the counts-containing return aggregate after store() committed. MSVC std::map move constructs a heap sentinel and can throw, including for an empty map. Therefore a return construction allocation failure could violate the documented strong guarantee.",
  "primary_sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/microsoft/STL/blob/vs-2022-17.14/stl/inc/map#L163-L168",
      "finding": "map move is not noexcept and delegates to the tree move"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/microsoft/STL/blob/vs-2022-17.14/stl/inc/xtree#L908-L913",
      "finding": "tree move allocates sentinel/proxy before swapping"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/microsoft/STL/blob/vs-2022-17.14/stl/inc/xtree#L1919-L1924",
      "finding": "sentinel setup allocates a node"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/reference/zc-nrvo?view=msvc-170",
      "finding": "Optional NRVO can be disabled in VS2022 17.4+; mandatory C++17 prvalue elision remains"
    }
  ],
  "historical_evidence_correction": "The prior Linux noexcept-move probe and Linux/macOS test results were real but did not establish portable no-allocation map moves. Existing adapter validation records describe earlier revisions and are superseded for publication/exception-safety by this record. No prior Windows pass is claimed.",
  "fix": {
    "public_api_change": false,
    "numeric_model_change": false,
    "limits_weakened": false,
    "tests_skipped": false,
    "design": "Private noncopyable/nonmovable PendingStore reserves a null vector slot and owns the uncommitted snapshot/state. The full aggregate return object, including counts-map moves, is constructed before local destruction. Normal-return destruction publishes with unique_ptr assignment/swap; unwinding removes the slot and leaves old state untouched. All helper/API returns use C++17 same-type prvalues; optional NRVO is unnecessary.",
    "methods": "polynomial, limited_amplifier, highorder_amplifier; all existing store users retain their public interface"
  },
